1,-1],"rooms":[{"name":"fauces","box":[16,2,2,19,5,7]},{"name":"shop W1","box":[1,2,1,7,5,7]},{"name":"shop W2","box":[9,2,1,14,5,7]},{"name":"shop E2","box":[21,2,1,26,5,7]},{"name":"shop E1","box":[28,2,1,34,5,7]},{"name":"atrium","box":[10,2,9,25,5,20]},{"name":"tablinum","box":[13,2,22,22,5,25]},{"name":"cubiculum W-N","box":[1,2,9,8,5,13]},{"name":"cubiculum W-S","box":[1,2,15,8,5,20]},{"name":"cubiculum W-P","box":[1,2,29,7,5,38]},{"name":"cubiculum E-P","box":[28,2,29,34,5,38]},{"name":"cubiculum E-S","box":[27,2,15,34,5,20]},{"name":"culina","box":[27,2,9,34,5,13]},{"name":"triclinium","box":[12,2,42,23,5,46]},{"name":"storeroom W","box":[1,2,22,11,5,25]},{"name":"storeroom E","box":[24,2,22,34,5,25]},{"name":"storeroom SW","box":[1,2,42,10,5,46]},{"name":"storeroom SE","box":[25,2,42,34,5,46]}]}BUILD: villa-haiku: a Roman villa (domus/villa urbana), single storey around open courts. Recognisable elements: a symmetrical street front with a recessed entrance (fauces) between shuttered shop rooms; the atrium behind it, open to the sky, with a shallow rain pool (impluvium) under a square opening (compluvium) in the roof; the tablinum (study) facing the entrance across the atrium; a peristyle garden court behind, ringed by a covered colonnade of white columns, with formal planting, low hedges, a fountain and statues; rooms off both courts: the triclinium (dining room with couches on three sides), cubicula (small bedrooms), a kitchen (culina) with a hearth; terracotta tile roofs sloping inward to the courts, cream plaster walls with a red painted dado, mosaic floors, bronze lamps and potted plants.
